  <div class="lh-container">
<div class="page-wrap"><h1 class="main-title">Damages of Property</h1><h2 class="sub-title">Halacha 2</h2><div class="source-ref">Likutay Halachos, Choshen Mishpat, Part II &nbsp;|&nbsp; Hilchos Nizkay Mamon</div><div class="opening-law">The four primary categories of damage: the ox, etc. According to the Torah <em>uv&rsquo;yom habikkurim</em> [And on the day of the first fruits] (&sect;56) &mdash; that the wicked kingdom, which is the counterpart of the holy kingdom, grows stronger to gather and amass money, for there all the holy sparks are found, and therefore it grows stronger through the desire for money. But there is power in the holy kingdom to extract what it has swallowed, in the aspect of <em>&ldquo;a time when man ruled over man to his harm&rdquo;</em> &mdash; extracting all the holiness from them, and from this comes exceedingly exalted Torah. And the wicked kingdom is the kingdom of Haman-Amalek, which pursues the camp of Dan, the aspect of the holy kingdom &mdash; see there.</div><div class="section-header">Section 1</div><p>And this is the aspect of the primary categories of damage [<em>avos nezikin</em>] &mdash; they are the aspect of the wicked kingdom, which damages the money of Israel. For they grow stronger over the money in order to blemish it, because all the good is found there, as above. And therefore they are four &mdash; for the holy kingdom is the aspect of the letter <em>dalet</em> [numerical value four], and when the aspect of the <em>dalet</em> &mdash; which is the holy kingdom &mdash; falls and is blemished, from this emerges the aspect of four kingdoms, which are the wicked kingdom, the aspect of Amalek who is comprised of all four kingdoms, as is brought in the Torah <em>&ldquo;Misra d&rsquo;Sakinah&rdquo;</em> (&sect;30). Therefore they grow stronger over the money to damage it &mdash; for the rectification and completeness of the holy kingdom is through hating money and despising it utterly, as is brought there. And therefore, conversely, the kingdom of the <em>sitra achra</em> &mdash; which is the four kingdoms &mdash; grows stronger to damage the money of Israel: they grow stronger through the desire for money, through which they damage the holy abundant flow of Israel, drawing it into desire which is the <em>sitra achra</em>, heaven forfend. For the primary exiles are only through money, because there all the holy sparks are found, and they grow stronger to extract them outward through the desire for money and through what they rob from the money of Israel &mdash; for these are one and the same: their actual robbery and the intensification of desire upon Israel &mdash; for everything is in order to suck and receive from the holy abundant flow hidden in the money, as above. But there is power in the holy kingdom to extract what they have swallowed from their mouths, as above.</p><p>And this is the aspect of the requirement to pay from the best &mdash; as it is written: <span class="verse-inline">&ldquo;the best of his field,&rdquo;</span> etc. For all the good is extracted from them &mdash; and moreover, even all the sparks and good that had been among them previously are extracted, since through the good gathering together &mdash; by their having grown stronger and drawn in much additional good &mdash; the sparks previously there, which had been unable to come out, are now joined and connected and cleaved to this additional good. And afterward everything comes out from them &mdash; this is the aspect of <span class="verse-inline">&ldquo;a time when man ruled over man to his harm&rdquo;</span>: for through their dominion and growing stronger, only the evil remains with them without any good &mdash; for that is their downfall, since all the good departs from them. And this is the aspect of <span class="verse-inline">&ldquo;the best of his field and the best of his vineyard shall he pay&rdquo;</span> &mdash; all the good that had been captive among them must be paid and returned to its owners, to holiness, as above.</p><p>And this is the aspect of what our Sages of blessed memory said: the damaged party and the damager share in the payment, for the dead animal belongs to him &mdash; meaning the owner deals with the carcass [<em>neveilah</em>]. For the damaged parties &mdash; who are Israel, over whom the damagers who are the nations grow stronger through the desire for money, thereby damaging their money &mdash; must receive the dead carcass and deal with it in order to clarify the good and vitality within it: namely, the holy sparks of Israel&rsquo;s money that still remain in it. This is incumbent upon the owners, the damaged parties who are Israel &mdash; for to them alone belongs this power to clarify and extract the good from the dead and broken. They too are obligated in this, and it is fitting for them to bear some of the damage, as our Sages said: the damaged party and the damager share in the payment &mdash; for upon the damaged party too falls a portion of the financial obligation &mdash; meaning they certainly must rectify what they were drawn after until they were damaged. For we must guard ourselves from the harm, namely not to be drawn after the desires of the nations as above. And therefore when they did not guard themselves until they were damaged &mdash; namely the damagers grew stronger over them &mdash; they must deal with the dead carcass and clarify the good from it, meaning the money that remains in it, as above. And the remainder of the damage is extracted from the damagers, who are brought to court and must pay from the best &mdash; meaning all the good that was captive among them is extracted from them, as above.</p><p>And this is accomplished through the three judges [<em>dayanim</em>] &mdash; as our Sages said: monetary damage cases require three judges. For the three judges are the aspect of the three Patriarchs, who are the aspect of the three Pilgrimage Festivals [<em>shalosh regalim</em>], through which the Kingdom rises among them &mdash; and then the <em>sitra achra</em>, which is the wicked kingdom, is subdued, meaning the good is extracted from them, for they pay from the best, as above. And this is as explained above in the laws of judges &mdash; see there.</p><p>And therefore they are called <em>avos nezikin</em> [primary categories of damage] corresponding to the holy kingdom, whose primary completeness is through the three Patriarchs &mdash; this being the aspect of the three Pilgrimage Festivals, as brought in the Torah &ldquo;Misra&rdquo; mentioned above. And corresponding to this, measure for measure, the wicked kingdom receives from the <em>avos</em> of impurity, whose primary is the corpse [<em>meis</em>] &mdash; which is the <em>av ha-tumah</em> [primary source of impurity] &mdash; which is the aspect of Amalek, as is brought. And they receive from there, for he encompasses them all &mdash; as it is written: <span class="verse-inline">&ldquo;first among the nations is Amalek,&rdquo;</span> as Rabbainu of blessed memory wrote there. And therefore the wicked kingdom is called the four primary categories of damage.</p><p>And this is what the Mishnah says: <em>&ldquo;Not this one is like that one, and not that one is like this one&rdquo;</em> &mdash; for they are the aspect of the world of separation [<em>alma d&rsquo;piruda</em>], the aspect of <span class="verse-inline">&ldquo;and from there it separated and became four heads&rdquo;</span> &mdash; the opposite of the holy kingdom, which is the aspect of the <em>dalet</em> of <em>Echad</em> [one], the aspect of simple unity. And therefore there is no unity and equality among them &mdash; only separation and division, with no common denominator &mdash; except that their nature is to cause damage, and when they damaged they must pay from the best, as above.</p><p>And one may explain: the ox is the aspect of Yavan [Greece], who said <span class="verse-inline">&ldquo;write for yourselves upon the horn of the ox,&rdquo;</span> etc. &mdash; the horn of the ox precisely, the aspect of the ox which is the aspect of the horn. The pit is the wicked kingdom of Edom-Amalek, who is prepared for stumbling &mdash; for the pit is the aspect of <em>tichol Lilit</em>, the mother of the impure force of licentiousness, which is the aspect of Amalek, as is brought. The grazing animal [<em>mav&rsquo;eh</em>], which is the tooth, is the aspect of eating &mdash; the aspect of Persia: <span class="verse-inline">&ldquo;and it devoured like a bear,&rdquo;</span> etc.; also Media grew stronger over Israel through eating &mdash; in the days of Achashverosh &mdash; on account of their having benefited from the feast of that wicked one. And the fire is Babylon &mdash; Nevuchadnetzar who set fire to the Holy Temple. And none of them is &ldquo;prepared for stumbling&rdquo; like the pit, which is Amalek &mdash; the desire of absolute evil, who encompasses them all, as above.</p><p>And this is what our Sages said: if the Torah had written only <em>bor</em> and one of the others, we could have derived all from them &mdash; for the pit encompasses them all, being the aspect of the kingdom of Amalek who encompasses them all. And from him all the others are derived &mdash; for everything was learned from him, as Rashi explained on the verse <span class="verse-inline">&ldquo;first among the nations is Amalek&rdquo;</span>: that he partnered with Israel first &mdash; the parable of the scalding bath, etc. &mdash; one came and cooled it for others. Thus from him the others learned to harm Israel, heaven forfend. And the Gemara concludes that they were all written only to magnify the Torah and make it glorious &mdash; for in truth, through the four primary categories of damage, which are the four kingdoms, through them precisely the Torah will be magnified and made glorious. For afterward their swallowed good is extracted from their mouths &mdash; in the aspect of <span class="verse-inline">&ldquo;wealth swallowed he shall vomit up&rdquo;</span> &mdash; and from this comes Torah, which is called <span class="verse-inline">&ldquo;the wealth of nations.&rdquo;</span> Thus it is precisely through them that Torah is magnified.</p><p>And this is what our Sages said: <em>avos</em> &mdash; to teach us that there are also <em>toldos</em> [derivatives] &mdash; for these four kingdoms are the generals of the seventy nations. It follows that they have <em>toldos</em> &mdash; namely the seventy nations who spread out from them.</p><p>And this is what our Sages said: one who wishes to be a <em>chassid</em> [devout one] should fulfill the words of Nezikin [the tractates on damages]. <em>Chassid</em> &mdash; this is the aspect of Avraham the man of <em>chesed</em>, through whose merit the Kingdom is primarily elevated from the four kingdoms &mdash; in the aspect of <span class="verse-inline">&ldquo;and a throne shall be established through kindness.&rdquo;</span> And therefore he pursued the four kings, as written there in the Torah &ldquo;Misra&rdquo; mentioned above. And this is: <em>fulfill the words of Nezikin</em> &mdash; to subdue the four kingdoms, which are the four primary categories of damage &mdash; and then one is in the aspect of <em>chassid</em>, the aspect of Avraham the man of <em>chesed</em>, as above.</p><p>And this is also what was said: <em>to fulfill the words of Avos</em> [the tractate Avos] &mdash; it is the same matter. For the completeness of the Kingdom is through the Patriarchs, as above.</p></div>
